Summary:  
Class 0 (No postpartum depression) tends to have happy feelings about motherhood, good relationships with husband and in-laws, no fear of pregnancy, good relationship between father and newborn, and typical pregnancy lengths (9-10 months). Class 1 (postpartum depression) tends to have sad or neutral feelings about motherhood, fear of pregnancy, worse relationships with in-laws or husband, and sometimes neutral or bad relationship between father and newborn.

